      {
        "met_days": 205.01,
        "type": "edl_or_oi",
        "label": "Mars orbit insertion",
        "description": "27-minute main-engine burn on 2021-02-09 captured Hope into an initial 40-hour capture orbit; the ~20,000 × 43,000 km science orbit came later. Hope is the first Mars mission to study the planet's lower atmosphere + weather + dust storms from a high-altitude 55-hour orbit — a vantage point that complements the lower-orbit science missions (MAVEN, TGO) it shares the Mars system with."
      }
